WEBVTT

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.000
I'm Bob.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.890
I'm Bob Ross, and for the next 13 weeks,

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.800
I'll be your host as we experience the joy of painting.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.840
This is a fantastic method of painting

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.140
where we use a wet-on-wet technique.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.100
And before I go far into the show,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.060
I'd like to take a few minutes and make a dedication.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.090
I would like to dedicate this show

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.890
to my beloved friend and teacher,

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:53.730
whom we've all watched and loved for many years

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.900
on public television, Bill Alexander.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.000
And years ago, Bill taught me this fantastic technique

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.830
technique, and I feel as though he gave me a precious gift, and I'd like to share that

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.230
gift with you.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:11.550
So before we start, let's talk a minute about the equipment that we'll be using here.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.450
We're using a stretch canvas rather than a canvas board.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:19.830
The canvas board will absorb your underpaint very rapidly and become dry.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:24.710
You need a strong easel, because we use a lot of pressure here, and you need an easel

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.210
that would grip the canvas and hold it securely.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.600
The pallet that we use.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:35.000
We use a large palette that has a lot of working area in it.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.410
And I'm gonna go over each of the colors that we use here,

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.110
and they'll be flashed across the screen.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.810
So if you need to write 'em down,

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.920
you can pick 'em up off the screen as I talk about 'em.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:45.760
So here we go.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.020
Let's start right up here with Titanium White,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:58.710
Phthalo Green, Phthalo Blue, Prussian Blue, Burn Umber,

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:07.080
Van Dyke Brown, Alizarin Crimson, Sap Green,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:14.500
Cad Yellow, Yellow Ochre, Indian Yellow,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.390
and Permanent Red.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.690
Now these 12 colors we'll use every week,

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.330
so if you want to have your palette ready,

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.220
these are the colors that we'll use.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.050
Also each week we'll run the colors across the screen,

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:28.340
so in case you didn't get all these,

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.960
you can pick them up the next time.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:34.810
The brushes that we use, these are natural bristle brushes, I'm using a two and a half

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.710
inch and a one inch brush.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:42.180
Also we use an almighty palette knife, a very big palette knife.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.640
And this palette knife, unlike traditional palette knives, is very firm, it's very big.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:51.160
So we can do almighty things very rapidly here.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.770
So let's do it.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.940
Let's paint an almighty picture right here.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:03:00.000
I'm gonna start by dipping the brush into a little bit of magic white.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.640
This makes the canvas wet, it makes it slick,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.270
it allows the paint to blend in here.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.020
You actually blend the painting on the canvas.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.360
So all we do here is cover the entire canvas

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.740
with a thin layer of the Magic White.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.040
Alright, probably the biggest mistake made

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.470
when you first start is applying too much Magic White.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:24.090
All we want is just a nice, thin, even coat.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.330
And when you're using large brushes,

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.820
this only takes a couple of minutes, so no problem.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:29.600
Here we go.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:38.280
Look at there, already we're almost complete.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.180
Okay, now just work it back and forth,

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:47.100
and up and down to get a nice even distribution of color.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:51.210
Okay, we just about got this canvas covered

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:57.040
with the magic white.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.000
Another big problem that we run into continually is washing

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.160
washing the brushes.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.780
Now, I'm gonna wash the brush,

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.710
and we wash it with odorless paint thinner.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.530
And I strongly suggest that you use odorless,

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.570
or you'll run everybody in the house out in the yard.

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.240
You'll be there by yourself.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.600
Now, we shake the brush into a box,

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.320
and then beat the bristles dry.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.720
Now, if you do this at home,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.120
this is a quick way to redecorate

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:24.800
your living room in a second.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.630
So be careful, learn how to contain this.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.700
Alrighty, let's do a simple little picture today.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.370
just give you an idea of how this fantastic technique works.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.360
So I'm gonna start here with a little bit of Prussian blue.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.800
And we pull a small amount of paint out

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.380
and beat it into the bristles.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.840
Really work this paint into the bristles.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.240
You're looking for a nice, even distribution of color

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.930
throughout the bristles.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.610
And we'll start right up here at the top,

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:52.160
and we just make little X's, little criss-cross pattern.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.540
Come all the way across the top.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.340
There we go.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.000
Now your brush is picking up the Magic White, and automatically

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.960
the sky is gonna get lighter in value

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:08.380
as it works toward the horizon.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.870
See how easy that was?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:16.730
Okay, and very gently, we'll just blend this out.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.810
Now it's very easy to make a sky darker,

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.030
but it's the son of a gun to make it lighter.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.350
If you want to make it a little darker,

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.820
all you do is add a little more blue.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.160
A little more blue.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.120
This stuff is really strong.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.000
And go right back through the same

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.570
procedure, and you can darken this guy very easily.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:39.500
Alright, another thing that seems to give us a lot of

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.480
problems is almighty clouds.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.740
So let's spend a second here and make us a cloud.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.180
And here we'll use the fan brush, and I'm gonna take

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:53.550
the fan brush and load it full of titanium white paint.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:58.490
Load it full, a lot of paint in the bristles.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.000
Okay now, we'll go up here.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.260
Go up here and decide where we want

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.230
a happy little cloud to float around.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.690
And you touch the canvas and just make little tiny circles.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:10.590
Just work it, work it, work it.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.230
Do it rapidly, push hard and get away from it.

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.650
Don't keep working the same area,

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:18.800
all you'll have is a big cotton ball up in the sky.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.700
Okay, maybe we'll put another little cloud right over here.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:27.580
Just to show you how to make these little clouds.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.000
Okay, now, with a large brush,

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.120
We want to very gently blend this out

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.610
on the bottom down here,

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.880
but without touching the top at all.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:39.340
So very gently, just the bottom.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.780
Just blend it a little bit.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:45.610
Little tiny circles.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.450
There we go.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:50.830
Now over here we'll blend this one a little.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:52.190
Now we'll fluff it,

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:55.480
and we're just gonna gently lift upward.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.580
And don't worry if you get some of these

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.040
little things up in the sky.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:05.980
Okay, very gently, we'll hypnotize that.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.840
There we go.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.650
These are very simple, very basic little clouds,

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:13.010
and very easy to do.

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.810
Now if you brush sheds like you just did here,

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:16.270
and you get a hair on you,

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.540
just take the corner of your brush and lift it off.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.080
Don't spend all day trying to pick it off.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.530
You'll have fingerprints all over your painting.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.510
Just use a corner of your brush.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:30.000
All right, let's now make

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.350
an almighty mountain.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.690
Everybody likes mountains,

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.790
no matter if you live in Florida or Alaska.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.600
Mountains are still pretty.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.470
I'm gonna take a little bit of the Prussian blue,

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.650
some Van Dyke brown,

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.920
and a little touch of crimson.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:47.440
Very little crimson.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.090
And we'll mix that up real good.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:53.650
All you need to do here is

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:56.910
push this almighty knife right into the canvas.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.160
Just push.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:07.420
and really pushing the paint right into the fabric.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.440
All we're looking for is just a basic outline

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:13.950
for this mountain.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.850
And you may have noticed by now,

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.090
we use no patterns, we do no sketching.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:22.480
We let this flow right out of our heart onto the canvas.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.520
Now with a large brush, I'm just gonna pull this down.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.650
One thing about mountains when you're painting 'em,

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.000
they should always be more distinct

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.920
at the top than they are at the bottom.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:34.900
'Cause at the bottom of the mountain we have mist

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:36.890
and now we have pollution.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.510
All of these things diffuse and break up light

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.550
and create the mist at the bottom of the mountain.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.590
So once again, we allow the Magic White

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.810
to mix with the paint and this happens automatically.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.960
We don't have to worry about it or think about it.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.400
Let it happen.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:56.830
Alright, let's put some snow on this almighty mountain.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:00.000
We'll use a little of the Titanium White and we're gonna

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.590
Start right up here on this peak.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:05.620
Just let this paint flow right down the mountain.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.160
And you want the paint to break like this,

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.970
so it creates all the little rocks and stones

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:14.570
and highlights and shadows in your mountain.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:26.130
There, light's gonna strike right along this peak also.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:29.020
And maybe just a little touch back in here.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.330
Now let's build some shadows.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:36.200
And we'll just use a little bit of the Prussian blue

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:45.030
and white, maybe a touch more, there we go.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:47.510
Now the shadows will run in the opposite direction.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:49.940
We'll start here and just let the shadows

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:53.640
run right across like this.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:10:00.000
There comes the shadow.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.840
and we've decided this peak is behind the mountain.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:07.590
So all we do is take this shadow and bring it right through.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:10.560
And automatically, you've just pushed a mountain around.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.350
On this canvas, you're the creator.

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:15.940
Anything that you want, you can build here.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:17.250
This is your world.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.150
Your dreams come real here.

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.430
Alright, there.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:29.000
Maybe we'll add just a couple more little peaks in here.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.000
Maybe there's a happy place.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:37.150
the peak right here.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:41.900
Put the highlight in first,

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:46.360
and then we give him his own private little shadow right there.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:49.630
Now this is a very basic, simple little mountain.

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:50.910
And as the series progresses,

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:52.750
we'll do some that are a little more complicated

00:10:52.750 --> 00:11:00.000
if this is too easy for you.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.090
Now, as we had talked about earlier,

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.010
we always want it to be more distinct on the top

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.550
than it is on the bottom.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:08.350
So, using the large brush here,

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.590
I'm gonna very gently tap the bottom of the mountain.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.980
I'm tapping, all I wanna do is diffuse.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.530
I don't wanna destroy it.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:24.790
Always following the angles.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:28.550
Now, very gently lift upward using the brush flat.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:36.970
Look at that, look at that mist.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:40.690
See, I knew you could do it.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:43.420
All right, I think it's time we had some fun now.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:45.080
Let's get over here into the sap green

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:47.020
and just load this brush full of paint.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:50.400
Just put a lot of paint into the brush.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.260
Just really work it into the bristles.

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:56.410
And we're gonna go right along here

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:58.730
and touch and push, just push.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.740
Just like so.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.420
This is where you need the almighty easel

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.060
because you're really pushing hard here.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:17.280
You're pushing the paint right into the fabric.

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:18.640
Just push it in.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:21.080
This is just straight sap green.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.620
And you're bending the bristles.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:28.160
Most important that you bend the bristles.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.630
Now, I'm gonna go into just a tiny bit of Prussian blue,

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:40.500
and we'll darken the front here.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.820
As things get closer to you in the landscape,

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:48.320
they should get darker in value.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.990
You know, while I'm doing that,

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.790
one of the most interesting things

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:54.030
that we see as we run across the country

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:57.490
teaching this fantastic method is people continually say,

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.810
"I can't draw a straight line.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.000
"I don't have the talent

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:02.250
to help Bob to do what you're doing.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.890
That's baloney.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.530
Talent is a pursued interest.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.890
In other words, anything that you're willing to practice,

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:13.050
you can do, and this is no exception.

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:14.350
But it's like driving the car.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.710
At first, it's a little difficult.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:17.010
You have to learn how to make your hands

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.590
and your foots work together.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.840
Same thing, and that's what we're trying to teach you here,

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.740
is the technique.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:26.880
Once you have the technique down,

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.260
all you need is a dream in your heart

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.890
and a desire to put it on canvas.

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:37.530
Okay, now, let's go back here in the background a little bit,

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:43.360
and we'll mix up some blue, this is Prussian blue,

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:47.100
brown, Van Dyke brown in about equal parts,

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:50.530
and sap green, all three of these are in about equal parts.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:55.530
And it should look very dark, it should look black on your palette.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.840
Okay, now with the fan brush here,

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.570
We'll make some, let's make some little evergreens

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.170
back here in front of this almighty mountain.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.630
And there's many, many ways to make them

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.130
and we'll try to show you a bunch of ways

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:10.280
during this series.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:13.040
Okay, we load the fan brush full of paint

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.120
and decide where you want your tree to be.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:19.060
You touch the canvas, turn the brush sideways,

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:23.110
and just begin building a tree, back and forth.

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:26.060
Isn't that easy?

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:28.060
Look at there.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:30.000
And trees get lonely too, they need a little

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.920
So we'll give him a friend right here.

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:39.030
And you know, sometimes you don't want to have

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:40.030
a bunch of distinct trees.

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.030
You just want indications of trees.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:42.950
So watch right here.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.060
This is the way to make indications.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:48.740
All we're doing is touching, just touching.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:53.900
And this looks like little trees when the painting's finished.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.900
They're way back in the background.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:59.510
And maybe over here.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:06.820
Just drop these in, this is such a free style of painting.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:12.810
Maybe there's some here that are a little closer.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.580
And we'll just drop them in.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.920
Let them just fall right off your fan brush.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:26.530
There we go.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:27.990
And we'll put a little more dark in here.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:30.000
You need dark in order to show light,

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:33.940
Here I'm just applying a little dark color.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:37.390
Now, another golden rule that you need to remember here.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.310
A thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:43.050
So I'm adding just a touch of Magic White on my brush here

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.160
to go through this thicker paint.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:46.480
And this will make it a little bit thinner

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:48.160
so it'll stick on top of the thick paint.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:52.410
This is why we're able to paint wet on wet.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.250
Okay, now let's put some happy little things

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.400
happening back in here.

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.060
Just some little bushes and stuff.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.000
Here they come.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:02.690
Just let 'em progress.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:15.340
Look at all them little rascals.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:22.860
Okay, with the knife here, I'm just using the point.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.980
Now scratch a few little trunks here and there.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:30.000
Already it looks like we have a multitude of trees and stuff

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.050
stuff back here.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:36.620
Okay, now let's move a little forward in the painting.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.550
And I'm gonna come right about here.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:40.820
There we go.

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:44.130
And we'll drop a bigger tree in here.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:46.130
There he goes.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:51.040
There he is.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:52.680
These little trees live in your fan brush

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.290
and you have to scare them out sometime.

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:04.570
I knew you could do it.

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:07.140
Just let that come right on there.

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:09.060
There's some trees on the other side over here, too.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:12.280
Let's put an almighty tree right here.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:14.800
We're having such a lot of fun doing these trees.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:26.550
We might as well just keep going with them.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:27.550
And by now you're probably saying,

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.830
"Hey, can he do anything but evergreens?"

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:33.760
let's do some different types of trees.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.520
And we'll take a one inch brush

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.950
and load some of the same color on it here.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:44.260
And let's put in some leafy trees.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:46.330
Just push them right off your brush.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:50.220
Bend the bristles, most important that you bend the bristles.

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:55.180
So you get all the actions that happen there.

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:57.200
And maybe over here a nice little tree.

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:09.420
Now, let's put a little trunk in here.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:12.660
I'll use a little bit of burnt umber.

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:19.420
Let's just lay some happy little trunks.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:25.590
The green trees, just here and there.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:30.000
There we go.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.890
in this big ol' tree over here.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:35.540
Like so, one in there.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.220
You can also take just the point of your knife

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.500
and scratch right through the paint

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:47.790
and put all kind of little indications in here.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:52.190
More of the thin paint to thin this down,

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:55.120
and we'll put some happy little highlights on there.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:57.600
Maybe we'll say this is, this looks like fall,

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.440
so let's use some bright colors here.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:04.800
They show up good on your set at home.

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:17.970
Look at that son of a gun.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:21.850
Alright, now, down in the bottom down here,

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:24.560
we need some nice little bushes that are happening.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:25.880
One thing to be very careful of,

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:27.220
don't kill all your dark areas.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.000
If you kill 'em, your painting becomes very flat.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:39.840
There we go.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:45.570
Maybe there's a happy little bush right here.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:46.630
Big ol' one here.

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:56.160
Big tree here.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.260
Somethin' underneath here.

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:58.680
Just to give it a little more depth.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:05.990
There we go.

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:09.530
We'll cut a few more little sticks and twigs here and there.

00:20:09.530 --> 00:20:11.840
And this helps create depth in the painting.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.950
It shows different planes.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:15.090
The more planes you can show,

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.450
the deeper the painting will be.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:21.930
So we'll just cut a few of them in here.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.320
You know, it's interesting.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.890
I was doing this painting one time at a mall,

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:27.670
and I had a man come along and he says,

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:29.710
"You know, I've been to that location."

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:30.000
He says,

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.740
Except it had a little pond right here.

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:33.080
He says, "If it had a little pond there,

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.900
"I'd buy that painting from you."

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.530
So I told him, I said, "You start writing the check,

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.150
"and by the time a check's done, you'll have a little pond.

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.790
"So watch right here, let's see what happens.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:48.910
"All you do is take this almighty brush and pull down,

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:51.950
"and we'll create a little pond right there.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:21:00.000
"It's that easy, there we go."

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.460
I'm gonna take a little bit of Prussian blue

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:04.630
just to make this pond a little bit deeper.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:08.240
I wanna have enough room for the trout to live in here.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.670
Just a little bit deeper.

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:13.310
This is one thing that's so fantastic

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.550
about this style of painting.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.290
Right in midstream, you can change your mind,

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:21.060
you can completely, completely change a painting

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:22.700
in just a second.

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:23.900
And here I'm just pulling across

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:27.060
to make it look like water.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.960
Isn't that something?

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:30.000
Now, we'll take just a tiny bit

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.610
a tiny bit of the Magic White,

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:40.840
and we'll put a little water line in here.

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.520
Just act like you're trying to cut a hole

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:45.160
right through the canvas.

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:51.290
And let's take, and I sort of wiped out

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:52.450
a couple of these little bushes here,

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.310
so let's just put them back in.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:58.070
Maybe on each side there we have some nice little bushes.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:04.250
Okay, now I'm gonna add just a tiny bit

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.640
of the Van Dyke brown and the burnt umber

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:09.280
to this magic white to make it,

00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:12.400
it's a very, very thin paint.

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:15.050
And with that, we'll just take and pull down here

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:19.290
a little bit and make us a nice little bank here.

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:23.780
Just some ground for the bushes and trees here to sit on.

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:24.980
Don't want 'em to fall off in the water

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:27.830
and make a big splash.

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:29.830
That'd disturb that old trout that lives in there.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:37.560
but maybe highlight it with just a tiny bit of white.

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:39.620
And this is a very, very gentle touch,

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.270
just enough to get the paint to come off the knife.

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:49.090
There we go, isn't that something?

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:52.070
Now, with just a little touch more Magic White,

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:56.750
we'll put a little water liner on into here.

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:00.000
There it is, just enough to set

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:07.850
I'm gonna separate this.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:11.230
A few more little sticks here and there,

00:23:11.230 --> 00:23:15.300
just to break it up.

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:16.680
Maybe there's some little grassy things

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:19.500
that sort of work down onto the bank here.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.020
Just here and there, over here, more to be some.

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:25.000
What happens if you change your mind again?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.090
Son of a gun.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:28.110
Let's change it again.

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:30.000
I'm gonna take the big brush and go right back into this

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:37.260
dark color, begin pushing, like so.

00:23:37.260 --> 00:23:39.060
And we'll just add another plane to this painting

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:41.320
and make it even deeper.

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:42.620
Just push this dark in there.

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:48.040
Once again, we need the dark in order to show the light.

00:23:48.040 --> 00:23:50.430
Okay, now we got our dark in there.

00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:53.010
Now we can highlight it.

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.470
Little more of the thin white here,

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:57.590
so we can thin this down, it sticks nice and easy.

00:23:57.590 --> 00:23:59.050
We'll use a little yellow ochre.

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:02.480
mixed with a little cad yellow,

00:24:02.480 --> 00:24:03.880
and mix it on your brush.

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:07.780
That way you get a multitude of things that happen.

00:24:07.780 --> 00:24:09.040
Maybe a little of the permanent red.

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:13.550
Let's put, ooh, there's a little fireball.

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.540
That's a nice one.

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:19.330
Right on down through like so.

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:24.300
And just let these flow with the lay of the land.

00:24:24.300 --> 00:24:25.440
And put all kind of little,

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:26.950
look at all those little grassy things.

00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:37.400
It's just as easy.

00:24:37.400 --> 00:24:44.350
We'll just cut a few little sticks here and there.

00:24:44.350 --> 00:24:45.750
You know, one of the hardest things to do

00:24:45.750 --> 00:24:48.980
when you're painting is to know when in the world will stop.

00:24:48.980 --> 00:24:52.140
It's such a temptation just to add one more stick

00:24:52.140 --> 00:24:54.480
or one more tree, and there comes a time

00:24:54.480 --> 00:25:00.000
when you have to stop or you piddle it to death.

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:01.550
I'll stop on that one.

00:25:01.550 --> 00:25:02.810
I'll show you how to sign a painting.

00:25:02.810 --> 00:25:05.830
This is something that gives people a lot of trouble.

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:09.530
And I'm gonna dip, this is a number two script liner,

00:25:09.530 --> 00:25:12.470
and I'm gonna dip it into a little bit of thin oil,

00:25:12.470 --> 00:25:15.550
and then use the liner brush,

00:25:15.550 --> 00:25:18.100
and make the paint so it's like water.

00:25:18.100 --> 00:25:20.790
Very, very thin, and it'll flow right on top of there.

00:25:20.790 --> 00:25:23.240
And turn this brush, twist it.

00:25:23.240 --> 00:25:27.620
That brings it to a nice, firm, sharp point.

00:25:27.620 --> 00:25:30.000
Okay?

00:25:30.670 --> 00:25:34.080
Let's sign it right here.

00:25:34.080 --> 00:25:38.100
All we do is touch and just let this paint flow

00:25:38.100 --> 00:25:41.580
right off this little liner brush.

00:25:41.580 --> 00:25:43.750
There we go.

00:25:43.750 --> 00:25:45.770
And luckily I have a very simple name.

00:25:45.770 --> 00:25:47.790
It's easy to spell and it only takes a second

00:25:47.790 --> 00:25:52.120
to sign a painting.

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:55.770
Now next week, I hope you have your canvas on your easel

00:25:55.770 --> 00:25:58.350
and you're all ready to go with us.

00:25:58.350 --> 00:26:00.000
We'll be doing a white canvas next week,

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:02.760
During the series, we're gonna do numerous different things.

00:26:02.760 --> 00:26:05.860
There'll be several paintings that we do on a black canvas.

00:26:05.860 --> 00:26:08.620
Oh, there'll be some that you won't believe.

00:26:08.620 --> 00:26:11.630
But next week, have a white canvas ready,

00:26:11.630 --> 00:26:15.810
you have the colors, and we'll be looking for you here.

00:26:15.810 --> 00:26:19.330
And until then, from all of us here,

00:26:19.330 --> 00:26:21.310
we'd like to wish each and every one of you

00:26:21.310 --> 00:26:24.610
happy painting, and God bless.
